{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause established, and it INVERTS the proposed fix. Do not swap the hash.\n\nMeasured on this host (macOS 26.6.2, `arm64`), in a worktree venv built by `make venv` +\n`make install`:\n\n```\n.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pypandoc_binary-1.17.dist-info/WHEEL\n  Tag: py3-none-macosx_11_0_arm64          <- the ARM64 wheel IS the one installed\nfile .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pypandoc/files/pandoc\n  Mach-O 64-bit executable x86_64          <- but the binary inside it is x86_64\nshasum -a 256 <that binary>\n  d7b1e75cd20ee6a788a1399492be07d4559949e18e55f34cfc5c91807fdfa90d\n```\n\nThat hash is EXACTLY the value pinned under `darwin-arm64` in\n`scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:60-63`. So the pin is not a copy-paste slip and\nit is not internally inconsistent: it faithfully records the binary that\n`pypandoc-binary==1.17` actually installs on Apple silicon. The defect is upstream —\nthe `macosx_11_0_arm64` wheel bundles an x86_64 pandoc. The two macOS wheels in `uv.lock`\ndiffer by one byte in size (25553945 vs 25553944), which is consistent with both carrying\nthe same x86_64 executable.\n\nConsequence: replacing the pin with the genuine arm64 hash\n`140353e19f2518a76aa144ce90a7afcb6f485ba94d0dbe069e77c805277908c3` would make the\nprovenance check describe a binary that `uv sync` never installs, so the check would begin\nFAILING on arm64 instead of passing. The hash swap alone makes things worse.\n\nThe live symptom is not a provenance mismatch but an exec failure, because this host has no\nRosetta:\n\n```\nOSError: [Errno 86] Bad CPU type in executable: .../pypandoc/files/pandoc\n```\n\n`pypandoc` then falls back, and 17 tests fail in `make verify` on every arm64 Mac:\n13 in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py`, 3 in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py`, 1 in\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_diff_comments_cutover_neutral.py`.\n\nVerified pre-existing and independent of any source change: a worktree at `origin/main`\n(8f7417079ad) carrying only a docs edit fails the same 13 in `test_wiki_render.py`. CI is\nunaffected, since the gating cell is `ubuntu-latest` and the linux x86_64 wheel runs\nnatively — so this never reddens `Verified`, only every local `make verify` on Apple\nsilicon, which is what makes it expensive.\n\nThere is no system pandoc on this host to fall back to (`which pandoc` is empty,\n`/opt/homebrew/bin/pandoc` absent).\n\nThis now needs a decision rather than a patch, because each option changes the provenance\ncontract differently. Recorded for the operator; not acting unilaterally."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789873647538969030,"uuid":"123e969a-9e07-41bd-a1af-9ef1da6cfd43"}